      <th width="22%", style="text-align:center">\({@x12*y12@}\)</th>
  </tr>  
  <tr>
      <th width="17%", style="text-align:center">\(\sum x={@sum_x@}\)</th>
       <th width="22%", style="text-align:center">\(\sum x^2={@sum_x_sq@}\)</th>
       <th width="17%", style="text-align:center">\(\sum y={@sum_y@}\)</th>
       <th width="22%", style="text-align:center">\(\sum y^2={@sum_y_sq@}\)</th>
      <th width="22%", style="text-align:center">\(\sum xy={@sum_xy@}\)</th>
  </tr>  
 </table>
<ol>
<li>
<p>\(n=12\)</p>
<p>The equation of regression line \(y\) on \(x\) is given by \(\hat{y}=\hat{\alpha}+\hat{\beta} x\).</p>
<p>where \(\displaystyle \hat{\alpha}=\frac{\sum y \sum x^2-\sum x \sum xy}{n \sum x^2-(\sum x)^2}=\frac{({@sum_y@}) ({@sum_x_sq@})-({@sum_x@})({@sum_xy@})}{12({@sum_x_sq@})-({@sum_x@})^2}={@alpha@}={@decimalplaces(alpha,2)@}\)</p>
<p>and</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \hat{\beta}=\frac{n\sum xy -\sum x \sum y}{n \sum x^2-(\sum x)^2}=\frac{12({@sum_xy@})-({@sum_x@})({@sum_y@})}{12({@sum_x_sq@})-({@sum_x@})^2}={@beta@}={@decimalplaces(beta,2)@}\)</p>
<p>Therefore, the equation of the regression line is given by: \(\hat{y}={@decimalplaces(alpha,2)@}+{@decimalplaces(beta,2)@} x\)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>\(\hat{y}={@decimalplaces(alpha,2)@}+{@decimalplaces(beta,2)@} ({@x13@})\)</p>
<p>Therefore, the total cost will be \(Ksh {@ta3@}\)</p>
</li>
<ol>]]></text>
